## 2. TECH STACK & BROWSER-NATIVE AI ARCHITECTURE
- **Frontend Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router), React 18+, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion, Lucide Icons, Recharts, Zustand.
- **In-Browser Computer Vision & Sensor Engine:**
  - `@mediapipe/tasks-vision` (`PoseLandmarker` extracting 33 2D/3D world landmarks at 15–30 FPS via WebGL/WASM over HTTPS/localhost).
  - `OpenCV.js` for image pre-processing, ambient lighting estimation, and desk-setup focal-length geometry.
  - `TensorFlow.js` / Temporal State Classifier for sitting, standing, walking, repetitive factory motion, elderly postural sway, and exercise repetition recognition.
  - **W3C Browser Hardware APIs:**
    - `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia` for explicit webcam sessions with instant hardware track release (`MediaStreamTrack.stop()`).
    - `DeviceMotionEvent` & `DeviceOrientationEvent` (including explicit iOS `DeviceMotionEvent.requestPermission()` handler) for camera-free **Travelling & Walking Mode** via 3-axis accelerometer and gyroscope fusion.
    - `navigator.bluetooth` (Web Bluetooth API) + WebSocket Sensor Bridge for pairing optional posture wearables or smartwatches.
- **Background Continuity (Solving Browser Tab Throttling & DOM Limits):**
  - **Web Worker Heartbeat Clock:** Because browser Web Workers cannot access `HTMLVideoElement` in the DOM, run a dedicated Web Worker strictly as an unthrottled 10 Hz clock (`setInterval` posting `"TICK"` every 100 ms). The main thread listens for `"TICK"` and executes `poseLandmarker.detectForVideo(videoElement, performance.now())` so posture analysis never freezes when the user switches to VS Code, Word, or another browser tab.
  - **Cross-Browser Picture-in-Picture (PiP) Mini-Companion:** Support Chrome/Edge `documentPictureInPicture` API first, and automatically fall back to rendering the live skeletal HUD + status pill onto an HTML5 `<canvas>`, piping `canvas.captureStream(15)` into a hidden `<video>` element, and invoking `video.requestPictureInPicture()` for Safari and Firefox compatibility.
- **Offline-First Persistence & Cloud Backend:**
  - **Local-First Browser Storage:** Persist user profiles, calibrated baselines, 60-second telemetry rollups, comfort journal entries, and volunteer trial datasets in browser `IndexedDB` (with `localStorage` fallback) so the entire platform works 100% offline or serverless, syncing via a background retry queue when connected.
  - **Backend API & Database:** Python FastAPI + PostgreSQL + WebSockets for real-time cross-device synchronization.
  - **AI Coaching Engine:** LLM + Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) grounded in the user's PostgreSQL/IndexedDB movement history, comfort journal correlations, and verified OSHA ergonomic guidelines, with full voice and text support in **English (`en-IN`/`en-US`), Hindi (`hi-IN`), and Gujarati (`gu-IN`)** via Web Speech API (`speechSynthesis` & `SpeechRecognition`).

